{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "229a510c-9254-437f-a7bd-0e9f32175233",
    "name": "COS Platform API (Credit Origination Showcase)",
    "description": "Demonstrates the REST contract of the three runnable Spring Boot / WireMock services in cos-platform:\n\n- **cos-decision-service** (DRS) \u2014 `POST /v1/applications/evaluate`, port 8081\n- **cos-orchestration** \u2014 `POST /v1/applications/originate`, port 8082 (the public-facing origination API; calls DRS and the bureau mocks itself)\n- **cos-bureau-mocks** \u2014 WireMock stubs for all 6 bureaus from the Integration Workbook, port 9561 (normally called by cos-orchestration, exposed here too so you can poke each bureau contract directly)\n\nEvery request body/assertion in this collection is lifted directly from an existing passing test (DecisionControllerTest, PartyRuleEngineTest, OrchestrationEndToEndTest, or a wiremock/mappings/*.json stub) rather than guessed, so a green run here is a real signal.\n\nSet `JAVA_HOME` to the project's JDK 21 first (see repo memory / README), then from `cos-platform/`:\n```\n./gradlew :cos-bureau-mocks:run      # or run BureauMockServer's main() from your IDE\n./gradlew :cos-decision-service:bootRun\n./gradlew :cos-orchestration:bootRun\n```\nThe \"cos-decision-service\" folder only needs DRS running. The \"cos-bureau-mocks\" folder only needs the mocks running. The \"cos-orchestration\" folder's valid-origination request needs all three; its invalid-payload request needs only orchestration itself.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "decisionServiceBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8081",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "orchestrationBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8082",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "bureauMocksBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:9561",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "cos-decision-service (DRS)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Evaluate \u2014 Compliance screening clean (PEPs pass)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/evaluate",
              "host": [
                "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "evaluate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Minimal example of the Call-DRS contract: a single Compliance bureau response with isPEPsMatch=false. DRS computes Party.decisions.customerPEPsStatus from it. Mirrors DecisionControllerTest#evaluateReturnsPartyDecisions, so the assertion below is verified against the real engine, not guessed.\n\nRun standalone: `./gradlew :cos-decision-service:bootRun` (listens on :8081).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-1\",\n  \"parties\": [\n    {\n      \"partyId\": \"P1\",\n      \"partyType\": \"Consumer\",\n      \"bureauResponses\": [\n        {\n          \"bureauResponseId\": \"BR-1\",\n          \"checkType\": \"Compliance\",\n          \"isPEPsMatch\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('PEPs status resolves to APPROVE', () => {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.parties[0].decisions.customerPEPsStatus).to.eql('APPROVE');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Evaluate \u2014 KYC + credit + compliance all clean (party credit eligibility APPROVE)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/evaluate",
              "host": [
                "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "evaluate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Richer example touching 3 of the 6 bureau check types DRS reasons over: KYC (identity match + confidence), ConsumerCredit (bureau score band) and Compliance (PEPs). With no manual override, a confident identity match, a score of 800 and no PEPs match, Party.decisions.creditEligibility resolves to APPROVE. Mirrors PartyRuleEngineTest#partyCreditEligibility_noOverride_allCleanApproves.\n\nNote: DRS recomputes every Party.decisions field from the raw facts you send (bureauResponses, person, identifications, manual*Decision) \u2014 whatever you put under `decisions` on the way in is ignored and overwritten on the way out.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-2\",\n  \"requestType\": \"CREDIT_CHECK\",\n  \"isCancelled\": false,\n  \"manualCreditDecision\": \"NONE\",\n  \"productRequests\": [\n    {\n      \"productRequestId\": \"PR-1\",\n      \"requestedAmount\": 5000,\n      \"termMonths\": 12\n    }\n  ],\n  \"parties\": [\n    {\n      \"partyId\": \"P1\",\n      \"partyType\": \"Consumer\",\n      \"identifications\": [\n        {\n          \"identificationId\": \"I1\",\n          \"expiresOn\": \"2030-01-01\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bureauResponses\": [\n        {\n          \"bureauResponseId\": \"BR-KYC\",\n          \"checkType\": \"KYC\",\n          \"isIdentityMatch\": true,\n          \"identityMatchConfidence\": 97\n        },\n        {\n          \"bureauResponseId\": \"BR-CREDIT\",\n          \"checkType\": \"ConsumerCredit\",\n          \"numericBureauScore\": 800\n        },\n        {\n          \"bureauResponseId\": \"BR-PEPS\",\n          \"checkType\": \"Compliance\",\n          \"isPEPsMatch\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('party credit eligibility resolves to APPROVE', () => {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.parties[0].decisions.creditEligibility).to.eql('APPROVE');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Evaluate \u2014 Chaos: inject HTTP 503",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Chaos-Inject",
                "value": "503",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/evaluate",
              "host": [
                "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "evaluate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "X-Chaos-Inject is a test-only fault-injection hook (DecisionController, gated behind cos.chaos.enabled, OFF by default) used to exercise the orchestrator's own DRS error-handling without a proxy in front of DRS. `X-Chaos-Inject: 503` returns that HTTP status instead of evaluating.\n\nStart DRS with the property enabled to see this fire: `./gradlew :cos-decision-service:bootRun --args='--cos.chaos.enabled=true'`. With the default (disabled) config this returns a normal 200 instead \u2014 the header is simply ignored.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('returns the injected status when chaos is enabled', () => {",
                  "    if (pm.response.code !== 200) {",
                  "        pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(503);",
                  "    } else {",
                  "        console.log('cos.chaos.enabled is false on this server \u2014 header was ignored, got 200 as normal');",
                  "    }",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Evaluate \u2014 Chaos: inject timeout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Chaos-Inject",
                "value": "timeout",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/evaluate",
              "host": [
                "{{decisionServiceBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "evaluate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same fault-injection hook as the 503 example, but `X-Chaos-Inject: timeout` sleeps for 30 seconds \u2014 long enough to trip the orchestrator's read timeout when DRS is called through cos-orchestration. Only meaningful with cos.chaos.enabled=true on this server; raise this request's timeout setting in Postman if you want to see the 30s sleep through to completion rather than Postman's own request timeout firing first.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cos-orchestration",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Originate \u2014 Fresh consumer, FULL_ORIGINATION (full external-data cycle)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orchestrationBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/originate",
              "host": [
                "{{orchestrationBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "originate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The showcase's main entry point (Process Workbook: \"Triggered by an inbound REST request to the COS origination API\"). A brand-new consumer application with no bureau data yet: the orchestrator detects everything is missing, calls Northgate KYC, Meridian (ConsumerCredit), Sentinel (Compliance) and Clearbank (BankCheck) via the bureau mocks, feeds the results back into DRS, and resolves routing in a second DRS cycle. Mirrors OrchestrationEndToEndTest#freshConsumerApplicationResolvesThroughTheExternalDataRequiredCycle (identification 8001015009087 and account ACCT-GOOD both hit the bureau mocks' default success stubs).\n\nPrerequisites \u2014 all three need to be running:\n  1. Bureau mocks: `./gradlew :cos-bureau-mocks:run` (or run com.cos.mocks.BureauMockServer's main method) \u2014 listens on :9561\n  2. cos-decision-service: `./gradlew :cos-decision-service:bootRun` \u2014 listens on :8081\n  3. cos-orchestration: `./gradlew :cos-orchestration:bootRun` \u2014 listens on :8082 (this request's target)",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-E2E-1\",\n  \"applicationTimestamp\": \"2026-11-14T09:00:00\",\n  \"channel\": \"Online\",\n  \"countryCode\": \"GB\",\n  \"requestType\": \"FULL_ORIGINATION\",\n  \"customerType\": \"Consumer\",\n  \"hasCreditApproval\": false,\n  \"parties\": [\n    {\n      \"partyId\": \"P1\",\n      \"partyRole\": \"Applicant\",\n      \"partyType\": \"Consumer\",\n      \"person\": {\n        \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n        \"lastName\": \"Doe\",\n        \"dateOfBirth\": \"1990-01-01\",\n        \"nationality\": \"GB\"\n      },\n      \"identifications\": [\n        {\n          \"identificationType\": \"NationalID\",\n          \"reference\": \"8001015009087\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"addresses\": [\n        {\n          \"addressType\": \"Residential\",\n          \"line1\": \"1 Example Street\",\n          \"city\": \"Sampleton\",\n          \"postalCode\": \"AB1 2CD\",\n          \"country\": \"GB\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bankAccounts\": [\n        {\n          \"accountType\": \"Current\",\n          \"accountHolderName\": \"Jane Doe\",\n          \"bankName\": \"Example Bank\",\n          \"accountNumber\": \"ACCT-GOOD\",\n          \"branchCode\": \"123456\",\n          \"isPrimary\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"productRequests\": [\n    {\n      \"productRequestId\": \"PR1\",\n      \"productCode\": \"PERSONAL_LOAN\",\n      \"requestedAmount\": 5000,\n      \"termMonths\": 24\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('application resolves past EXTERNAL_DATA_REQUIRED', () => {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.decisions.applicationRouting).to.not.eql('EXTERNAL_DATA_REQUIRED');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('all 4 bureau check types were gathered', () => {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const checkTypes = json.parties[0].bureauResponses.map(r => r.checkType);",
                  "    ['KYC', 'ConsumerCredit', 'Compliance', 'BankCheck'].forEach(t => {",
                  "        pm.expect(checkTypes).to.include(t);",
                  "    });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('resolved in exactly 2 DRS cycles (1 to discover missing data, 1 to route)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().drsCycleCount).to.eql(2);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Originate \u2014 Invalid payload rejected without calling DRS or bureaus",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{orchestrationBaseUrl}}/v1/applications/originate",
              "host": [
                "{{orchestrationBaseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "applications",
                "originate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "An application missing all core fields fails the orchestrator's own request validation (Process Workbook's \"Validate Request Payload\" gateway) before it ever calls DRS or a bureau \u2014 no network dependency on cos-decision-service or the bureau mocks needed for this one. Every error carries code VAL01 (missing core field). Mirrors OrchestrationEndToEndTest#invalidApplicationIsRejectedWithoutCallingDrsOrBureaus.\n\nOther validation codes worth trying by hand: VAL02 (consumer applicant with no `person`, or a business application with no linked representative) and VAL03 (empty productRequests, or a non-positive requestedAmount).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"applicationId\": \"APP-INVALID\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200 (rejection is a normal response, not an HTTP error)', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('application status is REJECTED with only VAL01 errors', () => {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('REJECTED');",
                  "    pm.expect(json.errors.every(e => e.code === 'VAL01')).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
